<title>UK: Shell chairman in hospital.</title>
<headline>Shell chairman in hospital.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Royal Dutch/Shell Group on Friday said group chairman Cor Herkstroter had unexpectedly been taken to hospital.</p>
<p>Medical treatment and recuperation were expected to take some weeks, the oil giant added.  </p>
<p>Shell declined to say why Herkstroter, who is also president of Royal Dutch Petroleum, was hospitalised.</p>
<p>Royal Dutch owns 60 percent of the Shell Group. Britain's Shell Transport and Trading Co Plc holds the remainder.</p>
<p>John Jennings, who is chairman of Shell Transport and Trading, will for the time being replace Dutchman Herkstroter as chairman of Shell Group's committee of managing directors.</p>
<p>As announced earlier, Jennings will retire at the end of this month to be succeeded by Mark Moody-Stuart.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
